{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]It makes no difference [C#m]where I turn
[F#m]I can't get [E]over you and the [Bm7]flame still burns
[D]It makes no difference [C#m]night or day
[F#m]The shadow [E]never seems to [D]fade away[E]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
And the [A]sun     [F#m]don't [D]shine   [E][A]anymore[D][A]
And the [A]rains     [F#m]fall [D]down   [E]on my [A][D]door[A]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[A]Now there's no love
[Em7]As true as the love
[D]That dies untold[B7]
And the [A]clouds     [F#m]never hung so [D]low   [E][A]before[D][A]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
It makes no difference how far I go
Like a scar the hurt will always show
It makes no difference who I meet
They're just a face in the crowd On a dead-end street
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[A]These old love letters
[Em7]Well, I just can't keep
[D]Cause like the gambler says
[B7]Read 'em and weep
And the [A]dawn     [F#m]don't rescue [D]me   [E]no [A]more[D][A]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[E]Without your love     [C#m]I'm nothing at all
[D]Like an empty hall it's a [Bm]lonely fall
[E]Since you've gone     [C#m]it's a losing battle
[D]Stampeding cattle, they [Bm]rattle the walls[E]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[A]Well, I love you so much
[Em7]It's all I can do
[D]Just to keep myself from [B7]telling you
That I [A]never   [F#m]felt so [D]alone   [E][A]before[D][A]
{end_of_chorus}
